section: rts
synopsis: Occasionally sort nursery blocks when needed to improve cache locality.
issues: #27719
description: {
  GHC Allocates space in the nursery in block groups. These can be reordered
  for one reason or another during the lifetime of a program. If such shuffling
  happens too often it leads to bad cache locality and corresponding slowdowns.

  The RTS now keeps a rough count of those re-orderings, and once a nursery has
  been shuffled sufficiently for sorting to be worthwhile it will be sorted by
  block address.

  Deeper details are documented in
  Note [Nursery Block Chain scrambling] in rts/sm/Storage.c.

  Note that this doesn't prevent *fragmentation* of the the nursery. That remains
  as a problem for another day.
}
